-- When the operator restricted the account at the person's request (GDPR Art. 18, `erase restrict`): while it is set the pool keeps the account's data stored and takes nothing more. Deposits, raw parts, machine enrollment, and club joins are refused 403 `account_restricted`, and its rows leave every club board; telemetry batches naming the account roll into no row; and the account stops counting toward a cell's holder count (a cell only it holds stops serving; a shared cell above its floor keeps its totals, which relate to no identifiable person, Art. 4(1)). Its export, an erasure, the withdrawal sweep, and the retention sweeps still run. Milliseconds; null when the account is not restricted. No credential is revoked, so lifting it (set to null) restores the account whole.
ALTER TABLE accounts ADD COLUMN restricted_at INTEGER;
